    "For U6, leverage Spring XD's existing stream abstractions and integrate with Spark Streaming via a dedicated SparkXD bridge module rather than forking Spark code.",
    "Refactor Import Options in U8 by introducing typed configuration properties bound via Spring's @ConfigurationProperties instead of ad-hoc command-line parsing.",
    "Documentation artifacts (U5, U7) will be authored in AsciiDoc to align with the existing Spring XD documentation conventions.",
    "All new code will be covered by unit tests; integration tests will use an in-memory/embedded approach where feasible."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The estimator is an experienced Java/Spring developer with prior knowledge of Spring XD internals.",
    "A development environment, CI pipeline, and necessary dependencies (Maven/Gradle, JDK 17+, Spring XD source tree) are already available and configured.",
    "The Receptor API specification is stable and documented; no protocol reverse-engineering is required for U1.",
    "Existing module deployment code in Spring XD is reasonably modular, so refactoring in U2 will not require rewriting the entire deployment layer.",
    "Spark Streaming integration in U6 targets an already-supported Spark version, with no need to upgrade Spark itself.",
    "Documentation updates (U5, U7) do not require setting up a new documentation build pipeline.",
    "Effort estimates exclude organizational overhead (meetings, code review wait time) but include the developer's own code review pass.",
    "Effort is reported in productive work-hours, excluding breaks and unrelated tasks.",
    "No localization or translation work is required for the documentation updates."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Explore existing Spring XD codebase and runtime",
      "activity_description": "Review relevant Spring XD modules (stream/job definition repository, module deployment, import options) to gain context before implementing changes. Identify reusable components and integration points.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Receptor Java client (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement a Java client library wrapping the Receptor API, including request/response DTOs, HTTP transport layer, error handling, and unit tests covering happy and failure paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Refactor stream/job definition repository (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Extract module deployment concerns from the stream/job definition repository into a separate abstraction, leaving a clean persistence- and metadata-focused repository interface and implementation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Design and implement pluggable Runtime SPI (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Define runtime SPI interfaces, default implementations, and a discovery mechanism (ServiceLoader-style) that allows selecting implementations for CF, on-prem, Mesos, etc. Add a sample alternative implementation to validate the SPI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement persistent repository for streams (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Add a persistent backing store (e.g., JDBC/embedded DB) for stream metadata, including schema definition, DAOs, transactional save/load logic, and a recovery routine that can reestablish streaming pipes after failure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Integrate XD streams with Spark/Spark Streaming (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Create the integration layer that allows XD stream definitions to be deployed as Spark Streaming jobs, including DSL extensions, job submission path, and synchronization between XD stream lifecycle and Spark job lifecycle.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Parameterize Import Options (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Replace the generic --args mechanism with typed, named import options for the Sqoop/Hadoop source. Introduce @ConfigurationProperties-style binding, validation, and deprecation of the --args flag.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Documentation: escape quotes in Sqoop jobs (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Author AsciiDoc documentation explaining the double-escape pattern (\\\\N) required when submitting Sqoop jobs from XD, with examples and a troubleshooting note.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Documentation: nesting batch jobs and workflows (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Write user-facing documentation with examples showing how to compose nested batch jobs and workflows in XD, including a reference sample and best-practice notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run and extend integration tests covering stream deployment, persistence recovery, runtime SPI selection, and Spark integration paths. Fix any regressions discovered.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Code review, refactoring, and finalization",
      "activity_description": "Self-review of changes, minor refactorings for clarity, updating CHANGELOG/README, and ensuring consistent coding style across the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 180
  }
}
